  "summary": "Malicious code in @insiderintelligence/googleadmanager (npm)",
  "details": "The package's install hook (node index.js) loads lib/core.js, which runs an obfuscated beacon on install. It collects the local username (os.userInfo().username), hostname (os.hostname()), and the current working directory basename (process.cwd()), then encodes them into a DNS query of the form iadgm.\u003cusername\u003e.\u003chostname\u003e.\u003ccwd\u003e.\u003cunix_timestamp\u003e.oob[.]algamil7x[.]xyz and resolves it via dns.resolve4, exfiltrating host metadata to the attacker-controlled domain oob[.]algamil7x[.]xyz. The README falsely states the package makes no network requests.",
